WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.635
-As you all know,
Juneteenth was yesterday.

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:06.005
And here to help us celebrate is
one of our writers, Jeff Wright!

00:00:06.005 --> 00:00:08.241
-Happy Juneteenth, everybody!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:08.241 --> 00:00:11.077
-Oh, Jeff, I thought you were
gonna be here in person.

00:00:11.077 --> 00:00:12.945
-Sorry I couldn't be there
in person, Seth.

00:00:12.945 --> 00:00:14.680
But I will tell you all
some fun facts

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:17.517
and things you can also do
to celebrate Juneteenth.

00:00:17.517 --> 00:00:20.086
Now, Juneteenth is a day
to remember, literally,

00:00:20.086 --> 00:00:22.889
because Black people were freed,
but it took two more years

00:00:22.889 --> 00:00:26.091
for white people to "remember"
to tell us that we were free.

00:00:26.091 --> 00:00:27.860
So to celebrate, I say

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:30.163
take an extra two hours on break
every day.

00:00:30.163 --> 00:00:33.399
I say take an extra two years
on an assignment.

00:00:33.399 --> 00:00:37.603
I say, instead of showing up
to work, show up on video.

00:00:37.603 --> 00:00:40.740
Isn't that right, Seth?
-It feels like a trick question.

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:43.809
-After all, I don't think
anyone minds if I'm on video

00:00:43.809 --> 00:00:45.678
and you're in the studio
in your red sweater.

00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:48.081
-Jeff, I'm not wearing a red s--
What are you talking about?

00:00:48.081 --> 00:00:52.351
-[ Laughs ] Exactly.
I think so, too.

00:00:52.351 --> 00:00:54.087
-What? What is happening?

00:00:54.087 --> 00:00:55.621
-I'm gonna be honest
with you, Seth.

00:00:55.621 --> 00:00:56.955
This is a pre-taped recording.

00:00:56.955 --> 00:00:59.025
You crazy if you think
I'm gonna work on Juneteenth.

00:00:59.025 --> 00:01:00.493
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:01.895
-Jeff Wright, everybody.

